<!doctype html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#080711">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/dashboard.css?v=<%= File.mtime(File.join(APP_ROOT, "public", "dashboard.css")).to_i %>">
  <title>Spark Settings</title>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="container settings-page spark-settings-page">
    <% navigation_active = "settings" %>
    <%= render_partial("navigation", binding) %>

    <header class="settings-header">
      <div>
        <h1>Spark</h1>
        <div class="subtitle">The optional homework helper that runs on a llama.cpp server on your network.</div>
      </div>
      <span class="ask-status" data-ask-status>Checking Spark&hellip;</span>
    </header>

    <% if request.query["saved"] == "context" %>
      <div class="backup-message success" role="status">
        <strong>Spark context saved.</strong>
        Future replies and newly generated daily overviews will use these notes. Earlier answers are unchanged.
      </div>
    <% elsif request.query["saved"] == "1" %>
      <div class="backup-message success" role="status">
        <strong>Spark model saved.</strong>
      </div>
    <% elsif spark_error %>
      <div class="backup-message error" role="alert">
        <strong><%= spark_context_error ? "Spark context not saved." : "Spark model not saved." %></strong>
        <%= h spark_error %>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <section class="card calendar-settings-card">
      <h2>Connection</h2>
      <dl class="spark-settings-list">
        <div>
          <dt>Server</dt>
          <dd><%= spark_settings["url"] ? "<code>#{h spark_settings["url"]}</code>" : "Not set" %></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>API key</dt>
          <dd><%= spark_settings["api_key"].empty? ? "Not set" : "Set (hidden)" %></dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <% if spark_settings["url"] %>
        <div class="settings-actions spark-test-actions">
          <p class="spark-check" data-spark-check aria-live="polite"></p>
          <button type="button" data-spark-test>Test Connection</button>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </section>

    <% if spark_settings["url"] %>
      <section class="card calendar-settings-card">
        <h2>Model</h2>
        <% if spark_models.any? %>
          <% state_labels = { "loaded" => "ready", "sleeping" => "asleep" } %>
          <form method="post" action="/settings/spark">
            <label>
              <span>Model Spark uses</span>
              <select name="model" data-spark-model>
                <option value=""<%= " selected" if spark_settings["model"].empty? %>>Automatic (<%= h spark_default_model %>)</option>
                <% spark_models.each do |model| %>
                  <option value="<%= h model["id"] %>"<%= " selected" if model["id"] == spark_settings["model"] %>><%= h model["id"] %><%= " · #{state_labels[model["state"]]}" if state_labels[model["state"]] %></option>
                <% end %>
                <% unless spark_settings["model"].empty? || spark_models.any? { |model| model["id"] == spark_settings["model"] } %>
                  <option value="<%= h spark_settings["model"] %>" selected disabled><%= h spark_settings["model"] %> · not installed</option>
                <% end %>
              </select>
              <small>
                Automatic uses the model that's already running on the PC.
                Picking one that isn't running makes the next answer wait while
                the PC loads it.
              </small>
            </label>
            <div class="settings-actions">
              <a href="/settings">Cancel</a>
              <button type="submit">Save Model</button>
            </div>
          </form>
        <% elsif model_listing["key_accepted"] == false %>
          <p class="settings-intro">The server rejected the API key, so its models can't be listed. Check the key, then reload this page.</p>
        <% else %>
          <p class="settings-intro">
            Spark is offline, so the installed models can't be listed.
            Turn on the PC, make sure llama-server is running, then reload this page.
            Currently using: <strong><%= spark_settings["model"].empty? ? "Automatic" : h(spark_settings["model"]) %></strong>.
          </p>
        <% end %>
      </section>
    <% end %>

    <section class="card calendar-settings-card spark-context-settings">
      <h2>Parent-provided context</h2>
      <p class="settings-intro">Give Spark background Canvas doesn't provide, such as grade level, curriculum names, unit topics, or study preferences. These notes guide chat replies and daily email overviews. Current Canvas instructions take priority; notes don't create assignments or deadlines.</p>
      <p class="settings-intro">Notes are saved once in Spark settings and included in backups, not copied into conversation history. Anyone who can access EmberGuide can read and edit them. Your configured local model can use curriculum hints to prepare public search topics, but raw notes aren't attached to the external search request. Avoid secrets and unnecessary sensitive details.</p>
      <form method="post" action="/settings/spark">
        <input type="hidden" name="action" value="context">
        <label>
          <span>Student context</span>
          <textarea name="student_context" rows="4" maxlength="<%= SPARK_CONTEXT_NOTE_MAX_CHARS %>" placeholder="Grade 7. Explain one step at a time and ask the student to explain their reasoning."><%= h parent_context["student_context"] %></textarea>
          <small>Freeform background used across classes. Up to <%= SPARK_CONTEXT_NOTE_MAX_CHARS %> characters per note and <%= SPARK_CONTEXT_TOTAL_MAX_CHARS %> in total.</small>
        </label>
        <h3>Class context</h3>
        <% if context_courses.empty? %>
          <p class="settings-intro">Refresh Canvas to add notes for individual classes. You can save student context now.</p>
        <% end %>
        <% context_courses.each do |course| %>
          <% course_id = course["id"].to_s %>
          <details class="spark-course-context">
            <summary><%= h(context_course_names[course_id] || course["name"]) %></summary>
            <label>
              <span>Context for <%= h(context_course_names[course_id] || course["name"]) %></span>
              <textarea name="course_context_<%= h course_id %>" rows="4" maxlength="<%= SPARK_CONTEXT_NOTE_MAX_CHARS %>" placeholder="Curriculum and unit topics, textbook terminology, or teacher preferences."><%= h parent_context["course_context"][course_id] %></textarea>
              <small>For example: Unit 2 is proportional relationships. The teacher expects vocabulary definitions from the textbook. Applies only to this class.</small>
            </label>
          </details>
        <% end %>
        <div class="settings-actions">
          <button type="submit">Save Context</button>
        </div>
      </form>
    </section>

    <section class="card calendar-settings-card">
      <h2>Optional web search</h2>
      <p class="settings-intro">Enable <strong>Search the web</strong> when asking Spark. Spark uses local class data to identify the study topic or vocabulary list, removes known student and teacher names and configured credentials, then sends the generated request to an external web-search service. Raw grades, Canvas notes, and chat history are not attached. These steps cannot guarantee anonymity, especially for names Spark doesn't know. The generated search appears with the sources under <strong>Spark searched the web for:</strong></p>
      <p class="settings-intro">No API key or extra setup is required. Free service limits apply; Spark reports a search error if the web-search service is unavailable or its limit is reached.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card calendar-settings-card">
      <h2>Changing the connection</h2>
      <% if spark_config_source == "addon" %>
        <p class="settings-intro">Set <code>llm_url</code> and <code>llm_api_key</code> in the Home Assistant add-on Configuration tab, then restart the add-on.</p>
      <% else %>
        <p class="settings-intro">Set <code>LLM_URL</code> and <code>LLM_API_KEY</code> in <code>.env</code>, then restart EmberGuide.</p>
      <% end %>
      <p class="settings-intro">The server and key can't be edited here because EmberGuide pages have no login. Keeping them with the Canvas token means nobody on the network can redirect class data to another server. The model can be picked here because it only chooses between models already on that server.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <script src="/ask.js?v=<%= File.mtime(File.join(APP_ROOT, "public", "ask.js")).to_i %>" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
